0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":5813.0,"requests":11}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in the providers.py scope that BOTH 'openai'-keyed gates — the `cfg.base_url` builder registration in `__init__` and the `provider_name == \"openai\"` per-candidate endpoint-override special-case in `provider_factory` — must recognize the `openai-chat` qualifier, so the custom-endpoint builder/profile override fires on both the base_url and per-candidate-endpoint paths.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0789,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["providers.py:100 `if cfg.base_url: self._builders[\"openai\"] = self._build_openai`","providers.py:145 `if builder is None and provider_name == \"openai\" and self._endpoint_override:`","After normalization pydantic-ai's infer_model splits `openai-chat:` and calls provider_factory('openai-chat'), which matches neither the `_builders` key nor the `== \"openai\"` check","Plan says only 'Register the custom-endpoint provider builder for the explicit qualifier' without naming both gates"],"finding":"The plan normalizes OpenAI targets to `openai-chat:` but does not call out that ProviderSession has two independent 'openai'-keyed gates that must both accept the new qualifier: the `cfg.base_url` builder registration keyed `\"openai\"` in `__init__`, and the `provider_name == \"openai\"` per-candidate endpoint-override special-case in `provider_factory`. If normalization changes the provider name to `openai-chat` but only one gate is updated, the custom-endpoint builder/profile-override silently fails to fire on the un-updated path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe1120abc2f96547d","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope (providers.py bullet)","norm_id":"n8e3fc1f1f9a79453","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A per-class `endpoint` on a fallback candidate (model_for endpoint override, base_url unset) resolves to an `openai-chat:` target and the line-145 special-case no longer matches 'openai-chat', so rebar's OpenAI-compatible builder is bypassed and the profile override / structured-output withdrawal is lost.","cfg.base_url set with an `openai-chat:` target: the __init__ registration under key 'openai' no longer matches the incoming 'openai-chat' name."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Classify the `openai:` grader targets in src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml as in-scope (normalize to `openai-chat:`) or explicitly out-of-scope, and state why in the Scope section.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2875,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`grep` finds `model: openai:gpt-4o-2024-08-06` in plan-review-verifier/g7/finder/container/isf-finder, ticket-quality, completion-verifier, code-quality, spec-alignment eval specs","Plan Scope enumerates only anthropic_model.py, model_classes.py, providers.py, t